  "question": "求极限 $\\lim_{n\\to \\infty}\\sqrt{n}\\left(1 - \\sum_{k = 1}^{n}\\frac{1}{n + \\sqrt{k}}\\right).$",
  "answer": "$a_{n} = \\sqrt{n}\\left(1 - \\sum_{k=1}^{n}\\frac{1}{n + \\sqrt{k}}\\right)$",
  "ref_source": "textbook:puheping_math_contest_v2",
  "techniques": [
    "夹逼准则",
    "极限计算"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "s1",
        "text": "分析 各项分母均介于 $n$ 到 $n + \\sqrt{n}$ 之间，为统一分母，将它们做适当的放缩（取为 $n$ 或 $n + \\sqrt{n}$ ），极限式就可表示为定积分，利用夹逼原理就可求得极限."
      },
      {
        "id": "s2",
        "text": "记 $a_{n} = \\sqrt{n}\\left(1 - \\sum_{k=1}^{n}\\frac{1}{n + \\sqrt{k}}\\right)$ ，则"
      },
      {
        "id": "s3",
        "text": "a _ {n} = \\sqrt {n} \\sum_ {k = 1} ^ {n} \\left(\\frac {1}{n} - \\frac {1}{n + \\sqrt {k}}\\right) = \\frac {1}{\\sqrt {n}} \\sum_ {k = 1} ^ {n} \\frac {\\sqrt {k}}{n + \\sqrt {k}}."
      },
      {
        "id": "s4",
        "text": "显然"
      },
      {
        "id": "s5",
        "text": "\\frac {1}{n + \\sqrt {n}} \\sum_ {k = 1} ^ {n} \\sqrt {\\frac {k}{n}} <   \\frac {1}{\\sqrt {n}} \\sum_ {k = 1} ^ {n} \\frac {\\sqrt {k}}{n + \\sqrt {k}} <   \\frac {1}{n} \\sum_ {k = 1} ^ {n} \\sqrt {\\frac {k}{n}}."
      },
      {
        "id": "s6",
        "text": "而"
      },
      {
        "id": "s7",
        "text": "\\lim _ {n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac {1}{n} \\sum_ {k = 1} ^ {n} \\sqrt {\\frac {k}{n}} = \\int_ {0} ^ {1} \\sqrt {x} d x = \\frac {2}{3}, \\quad \\lim _ {n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac {1}{n + \\sqrt {n}} \\sum_ {k = 1} ^ {n} \\sqrt {\\frac {k}{n}} = \\lim _ {n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac {n}{n + \\sqrt {n}} \\cdot \\lim _ {n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac {1}{n} \\sum_ {k = 1} ^ {n} \\sqrt {\\frac {k}{n}} = \\frac {2}{3}."
      }
    ],
    "final_answer": "$a_{n} = \\sqrt{n}\\left(1 - \\sum_{k=1}^{n}\\frac{1}{n + \\sqrt{k}}\\right)$",
